{
  "category": "Snacks",
  "summary": "The Snacks category held only 3 items (cracker, tortilla chip, vanilla wafer) — a severe gap for a 2277-item catalog. Existing items are mostly well-formed (good facets/aliases), but vanilla-wafer is incorrectly tagged Gluten-Free (wheat-flour wafers are NOT GF), and 'cracker' is tagged Vegan/Dairy-Free although the dominant subtype (Ritz/butter crackers) contains dairy/butter and many crackers contain milk. Several snack-shaped items live in OTHER categories where they represent the raw ingredient, not the packaged snack: 'popcorn' = popcorn SALT (Spices), 'jerky' = cured meat (Protein), 'granola' = cereal (Grains), 'cookie'/'chocolate-chip'/'oatmeal-cookie' etc = home-baked cookies (Baking), 'raisin'/'currants'/'sultana' = baking ingredients (Baking), 'corn-nut' = Nuts & Seeds, 'nori-seaweed'/'dried-goji-berry' = Produce, 'pretzel' = pretzel BUN (Breads). These cross-category items are NOT duplicates of the packaged grab-and-go snacks consumers track, so I added the packaged-snack forms here (e.g. microwave popcorn, packaged granola bars, snack-pack cookies, packaged dried fruit, snack pretzels) and flagged the naming/placement ambiguity as issues rather than deleting. Added ~95 new packaged snacks spanning chips/crisps, crackers, pretzels, popcorn, snack bars, cookies/biscuits, candy/chocolate, dried fruit, trail mix, rice cakes, jerky/meat snacks, seaweed snacks, puffs, and globally-common packaged snacks.",
  "issues": [
    {"itemId": "vanilla-wafer", "issue": "Tagged Gluten-Free but classic vanilla wafers (Nilla) are made with wheat flour — NOT gluten-free. Remove Gluten-Free; add 'gluten' allergen. Also tagged Vegan though many wafer brands contain milk/whey — Vegan is risky; consider Vegetarian only."},
    {"itemId": "cracker", "issue": "Tagged Vegan + Dairy-Free, but its own facet list includes 'butter' and 'ritz' variants which contain butter/dairy; saltines are vegan but butter/Ritz/cheese crackers are not. The umbrella item shouldn't carry Vegan/Dairy-Free unconditionally. Consider scoping those tags to the saltine/oyster/wheat variants only."},
    {"itemId": "cracker", "issue": "Missing very common cracker types as variants/aliases: 'water cracker', 'cream cracker', 'matzo/matzah', 'club cracker', 'cheese cracker (Cheez-It)', 'flatbread cracker', 'rice cracker', 'multigrain cracker', 'animal cracker' (though animal crackers are arguably cookies)."},
    {"itemId": "tortilla-chip", "issue": "Well-formed but missing common aliases 'tostada chip', 'restaurant style tortilla chip', 'scoops', 'multigrain tortilla chip', 'lime tortilla chip'. The 'gluten' allergen on a pure-corn tortilla chip is questionable — most corn tortilla chips are gluten-free; gluten only applies to the 'flour' variant. Consider scoping the gluten allergen to the flour variant and adding Gluten-Free to the corn variants."},
    {"itemId": "popcorn", "issue": "ID 'popcorn' currently maps to 'popcorn salt' in Spices & Herbs. There is NO packaged popcorn snack in the catalog. New items 'microwave popcorn' and 'popcorn (ready-to-eat / kettle / caramel)' added here. The bare word 'popcorn' as a user input will currently match the salt — a relevance hazard."},
    {"itemId": "jerky", "issue": "ID 'jerky' = 'jerky cured meat' in Protein (raw-ish bulk). Packaged shelf-stable meat snacks (beef jerky pack, beef stick, meat snack stick, biltong, turkey jerky) are a distinct grab-and-go snack and were added here; flagged for possible alias cross-linking."},
    {"itemId": "granola", "issue": "ID 'granola' = 'granola cereal' (Grains). Packaged granola/cereal/protein BARS (a top snack type in the brief) do not exist anywhere — added as new items here."},
    {"itemId": "cookie", "issue": "All cookie IDs (cookie, chocolate-chip, oatmeal-cookie, sugar-cookie, shortbread, snickerdoodle, gingerbread, macaron, macaroon) live in Baking & Sweeteners and represent home-baked cookies. Packaged snack cookies/biscuits (Oreo-style sandwich cookie, digestive biscuit, biscotti, fig bar, animal crackers, wafer rolls) are a snack staple and were added here. Flagged as potential redundancy depending on whether the catalog wants to distinguish baked-from-scratch vs packaged."},
    {"itemId": "nori-seaweed", "issue": "Plain nori/seaweed sheets are Produce. The packaged 'roasted seaweed snack' (seasoned snack packs, e.g. gimMe/Annie Chun) is a distinct popular snack — added here."}
  ],
  "redundancies": [
    ["cracker", "vanilla-wafer", "Not duplicates, but both are packaged biscuit-type snacks; ensure vanilla-wafer isn't also reachable via a generic 'wafer cookie' alias on a new item — keep wafer-roll/sandwich-cookie distinct from vanilla-wafer."],
    ["popcorn", "microwave-popcorn", "Existing 'popcorn' (=popcorn salt, Spices) will collide on the bare token 'popcorn' with the new packaged popcorn items; needs disambiguation (rename existing to 'popcorn salt' as its display name already does, and ensure the snack items own the 'popcorn' aliases)."]
  ],
  "aliasAdditions": [
    {"itemId": "cracker", "add": ["water cracker", "cream cracker", "club cracker", "flatbread cracker", "rice cracker", "multigrain cracker", "cheese cracker", "cheez-it", "matzo", "matzah", "matzo cracker", "crispbread"]},
    {"itemId": "tortilla-chip", "add": ["tostada chip", "restaurant style tortilla chip", "scoops", "multigrain tortilla chip", "lime tortilla chip", "white corn tortilla chip", "totopos"]},
    {"itemId": "vanilla-wafer", "add": ["wafer cookie", "vanilla wafer cookie"]}
  ],
